Carafe Lab: under NCE an access the guest may not make goes to the process's exception handler as a data
abort with its address, as under the JIT, instead of skipping the instruction; the runtime commits reserved
memory and swaps pages in from these aborts. A fault on a page the guest maps but may not access that way is a
permission fault instead of a retry of the same instruction forever. An unaligned exclusive access, which the
PC's CPU faults on as the console's does and Eden's interpreter cannot run, is an alignment fault (DFSC 0x21),
which the runtime reports as a misaligned access. A read of a page the GPU caches first downloads what the GPU
wrote there, as the JIT's reads do since 0012; Eden only invalidated the GPU's copy, so the CPU read stale data
such as query results.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

